    {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Which ROC handles company name change in Mumbai?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"ROC Mumbai at Everest House, 100 Marine Lines, Mumbai 400020. Forms MGT-14 and INC-24 filed electronically on MCA V3 portal. RUN name reservation also on portal. ROC issues fresh Certificate of Incorporation (INC-25). Patron's office is adjacent to ROC Everest House."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What resolution is needed for company name change?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Special Resolution with 75% majority at EGM or postal ballot under Section 13. Stricter than ordinary resolution because it alters the MOA. EGM requires 21 clear days' notice (shorter with 95% consent). Patron drafts Special Resolution and conducts EGM."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the RUN service for name reservation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RUN (Reserve Unique Name) is MCA V3 portal web service to check availability and reserve proposed name. Rs 1,000 per application. One name per application. Approved name valid 60 days (INC-24 must be filed within this window). Patron files with pre-checked names."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does the name change process take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MCA filing phase: 15-25 working days. Post-approval updates (PAN, GST, bank, EPF, signboard): 15-30 additional days. Total end-to-end: 30-45 working days. With shorter EGM notice (95% consent): MCA phase compressed to 12-18 days. Patron fast-tracks for M&A deadlines."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens after the name change is approved?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Update new name across 12 registrations: PAN, TAN, GST, bank accounts, EPF, ESIC, FSSAI, IEC, signboard (mandatory Section 12(3)), letterhead/invoices, domain, and contracts. Old and new name displayed together on documents for 2 years. Patron manages complete checklist."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a company change name with pending filings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Under Rule 29(1), companies defaulting in filing with ROC or repaying deposits/debentures cannot change name. INC-24 will be rejected. Patron resolves defaults first (filing overdue forms with additional fees), then initiates name change."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the CIN change after name change?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. CIN remains the same. Only the company name changes on MCA Master Data and fresh Certificate of Incorporation. PAN number also unchanged (only name on PAN card updated). All existing contracts, litigation, and registrations continue under new name."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is trademark search necessary before name change?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not legally mandatory for MCA filing, but strongly recommended. A name passing MCA RUN check may conflict with a registered trademark. If trademark holder complains, ROC may direct re-naming under Section 16. Patron conducts Trademark Registry search before RUN for every Mumbai company."}}]}
    </script>
