<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Change in Name of Company in Mumbai &ndash; Overview</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Change in Name of Company Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>Changing the name of a company involves altering the name clause in the Memorandum of Association under Section 13 of the Companies Act, 2013. Mumbai companies frequently need name changes for: rebranding (BKC MNC subsidiaries aligning with global parent), startup pivots (Powai startups reflecting new business direction), M&amp;A integration (acquirer name adoption), trademark conflict resolution (ROC direction under Section 16), and product brand alignment (Andheri media/consumer companies). The process requires a Special Resolution (75% majority), RUN name reservation, filing Forms MGT-14 and INC-24 with ROC Mumbai, and a comprehensive 12-item post-approval update across PAN, GST, bank, EPF, signboard, and all registrations.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Mumbai has the highest number of company name changes in India, driven by the city's dynamic business environment. BKC MNC subsidiaries rebrand for global alignment. Powai startups pivot and rename. Fort holding companies restructure group entities. Andheri media companies rebrand around flagship products. The process involves multiple MCA filings and, critically, a comprehensive post-approval update across 10-15 registrations. Learn more about <a href="/change-in-name-of-company">Change in Name of Company across India</a>.</p>
                <p>Patron Accounting's Mumbai office at Marine Lines &ndash; adjacent to ROC Mumbai Everest House &ndash; provides end-to-end company name change: trademark pre-check, RUN reservation, EGM documentation, Special Resolution, MGT-14 and INC-24 filing, fresh Certificate of Incorporation tracking, and the complete 12-item post-approval update checklist. For ongoing compliance, see <a href="/private-limited-company-compliance">Private Limited Company Compliance</a>.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is a Company Name Change?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>A company name change is the legal alteration of the name clause in the Memorandum of Association (MOA) under Section 13 of the Companies Act, 2013, resulting in the company operating under a new name while retaining its legal identity, CIN, rights, obligations, contracts, and liabilities.</p>
                    <p>Changing a company name does not create a new entity. The company continues with the same CIN, the same PAN (name updated on card), all existing contracts remain valid, all pending litigation continues, and all assets and liabilities transfer seamlessly. The change is a rebranding at the legal registration level, requiring MCA and ROC approval. For <a href="/trademark-registration">Trademark Registration</a>, check that the new name does not conflict with existing marks.</p>
                    <p>For Mumbai companies, the process involves three phases: (1) Pre-filing: trademark check, RUN name reservation, board and shareholder approval; (2) Filing: MGT-14 and INC-24 with ROC Mumbai; (3) Post-approval: updating the new name across PAN, GST, bank accounts, and all statutory and operational registrations. The post-approval phase is often the most time-consuming and where many Mumbai companies face operational disruption if not managed systematically.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Change in Name of Company:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Section 13:</strong> Alteration of MOA including name clause &ndash; requires Special Resolution + ROC approval</li>
                        <li><strong>RUN:</strong> Reserve Unique Name &ndash; MCA web service to check and reserve proposed name, Rs 1,000, valid 60 days</li>
                        <li><strong>Form INC-24:</strong> MCA form for ROC approval of name change, filed within 60-day RUN validity</li>
                        <li><strong>Form INC-25:</strong> Fresh Certificate of Incorporation with new name, CIN unchanged</li>
                        <li><strong>Section 12(3):</strong> Display old + new name on documents for 2 years after change; signboard mandatory</li>
                        <li><strong>Rule 29(1):</strong> Companies in default cannot change name until defaults are resolved</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
            </div>
