<!-- SECTION 4: WHO CAN FILE -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">When Mumbai Companies Need a Name Change</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Rebranding and global alignment at BKC and Nariman Point</strong> &ndash; MNC subsidiaries rebrand when global parents merge, acquire, or restructure. Indian subsidiary must align with new global identity. Common at BKC where international banks, tech companies, and consulting firms operate.</p>
                <p><strong>Startup pivot at Powai and Andheri</strong> &ndash; Startups pivoting from original product/market rename to reflect new business direction. A Powai fintech pivoting from payments to lending, or an Andheri healthtech expanding from telemedicine to full-stack health, may rebrand. <a href="/change-in-authorised-capital">Change in Authorised Capital</a> often accompanies pivots requiring new investment.</p>
                <p><strong>M&amp;A integration</strong> &ndash; Acquired entity changes name to acquirer's brand. Common in BKC financial services, Andheri media buyouts, and Nariman Point holding company restructurings.</p>
                <p><strong>Trademark conflict resolution</strong> &ndash; ROC may direct name change under Section 16 when company name conflicts with a registered trademark. Mumbai companies in competitive sectors (tech, media, consumer) encounter this frequently.</p>
                <p><strong>Product brand alignment at Andheri and Lower Parel</strong> &ndash; Consumer and media companies whose flagship product/platform becomes more recognisable than the corporate name rename to match.</p>
                <p><strong>Group restructuring at Fort and Nariman Point</strong> &ndash; Holding companies and group entities renaming subsidiaries for clarity, tax efficiency, or operational streamlining.</p>
                <p><strong>Conversion (Pvt Ltd to Public or vice versa)</strong> &ndash; Converting company status also treated as name change under Section 13(2), requiring the same RUN + INC-24 process.</p>

            </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

