                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which ROC handles company name change in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>ROC Mumbai at Everest House, 100 Marine Lines, Mumbai 400020. Forms MGT-14 and INC-24 filed electronically on MCA V3 portal. RUN name reservation also on portal. ROC issues fresh Certificate of Incorporation (INC-25). Patron's office at Marine Lines is adjacent to ROC Everest House.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What resolution is needed for company name change?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Special Resolution with 75% majority at EGM or postal ballot under Section 13. Stricter than ordinary resolution because it alters the MOA. EGM requires 21 clear days' notice (shorter with 95% consent). Patron drafts the Special Resolution and conducts the EGM for Mumbai companies.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the RUN service for name reservation?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>RUN (Reserve Unique Name) is an MCA V3 portal web service to check availability and reserve a proposed name. Fee: Rs 1,000 per application. One name per application. Approved name valid for 60 days (INC-24 must be filed within this window). If rejected, fresh RUN required. Patron files with pre-checked names.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does the name change process take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>MCA filing phase: 15-25 working days. Post-approval updates (PAN, GST, bank, EPF, signboard): 15-30 additional days. Total end-to-end: 30-45 working days. With shorter EGM notice (95% consent), MCA phase can be compressed to 12-18 working days. Patron fast-tracks for M&amp;A deadlines.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens after the name change is approved?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Update new name across 12 registrations: PAN, TAN, GST, bank accounts, EPF, ESIC, FSSAI, IEC, signboard (mandatory Section 12(3)), letterhead/invoices, domain, and contracts. Old + new name displayed on all documents for 2 years. Company cannot use new name until certificate is received. Patron manages the complete checklist.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a company change name with pending filings?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Under Rule 29(1), companies defaulting in filing with ROC or repaying deposits/debentures cannot change name. INC-24 will be rejected. Patron resolves defaults first (filing overdue forms with additional fees), then initiates the name change process.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Does the CIN change after a name change?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. CIN remains the same. Only the company name changes on MCA Master Data and on the fresh Certificate of Incorporation. PAN number also unchanged (only name on PAN card updated). All existing contracts, litigation, and registrations continue under the new name with the same CIN and PAN.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is a trademark search necessary before name change?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Not legally mandatory for MCA filing, but strongly recommended. A name passing MCA RUN check may conflict with a registered trademark. If the trademark holder files a complaint, ROC may direct re-naming under Section 16 &ndash; repeating the entire process. Patron conducts a Trademark Registry search before RUN for every Mumbai company.</p></div>
